#: ../../adr/0025-declarative-components.md:1
msgid "ADR-0025: Declarative components, made by users without code"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0025-declarative-components.md:3
msgid "**Status**: accepted"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0025-declarative-components.md:4
msgid "**Date**: 2026-10-20"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0025-declarative-components.md:5
msgid "**Plan step**: P15.14 (also P15.15, P15.16)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0025-declarative-components.md:7
msgid "Context"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0025-declarative-components.md:9
msgid ""
"Users want to make their own components (a fibre coupler with its "
"measured matrix, an attenuator, a filter with its measured transmission) "
"and share them, from the web interface too (review of 19/10/2026). Python"
" code can already define elements (plugins, script blocks, ADR-0013), but"
" code cannot run on the public instance: running the code of a visitor "
"gives them the machine. The decisions of 20/10 "
"(`docs/specs/pistes_evolution.md`, §2) keep code to local and private "
"instances, and ask for **declarative** components, made with a form from "
"templates, valid everywhere, and a catalogue in a `community/` folder of "
"the repository."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0025-declarative-components.md:16
msgid "Decision"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0025-declarative-components.md:18
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"**A component is data**: a `.lumos` document of kind `component` holding "
"`{\"id\", \"version\", \"title\", \"description\", \"license\", "
"\"authors\", \"template\", \"params\", \"body\", \"checks\"}`. Unknown "
"keys are refused; nothing in it is executed, imported or unpickled."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0025-declarative-components.md:21
msgid ""
"`id`: `author.Name` (a lowercase author, a capitalised name); the element"
" type is `components.<author>.<Name>`, its type version is `version`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0025-declarative-components.md:23
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"`params`: the parameters of the component, `{name: {\"unit\", "
"\"default\", \"bounds\", \"doc\"}}`, as those of the built-in elements "
"(units, bounds, description), editable in the inspector and free for "
"studies."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0025-declarative-components.md:25
msgid ""
"`body`: the behaviour, given by the `template`; a value of the body is a "
"quantity (`\"3 dB\"`), a number, an array, or `\"$name\"`, the value of a"
" parameter."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0025-declarative-components.md:27
msgid "**Templates** (decided on 20/10):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0025-declarative-components.md:28
msgid ""
"`transfer_matrix`: a matrix of moduli and phases at a wavelength, "
"achromatic or with optical paths, on a bus of guided lanes (the behaviour"
" of `TransferMatrix`), refused if it amplifies;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0025-declarative-components.md:30
msgid ""
"`gain_phase`: a power gain (at most 1 unless `amplifier` is true) and a "
"phase on any optical signal, lane by lane on a bus;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0025-declarative-components.md:32
msgid ""
"`spectral_transmission`: a tabulated power transmission `T(λ)` (linear "
"interpolation, 0 outside the table) on any optical signal with "
"wavelengths;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0025-declarative-components.md:34
msgid ""
"`composite`: a group (the entry of a `.lumos` group), placed as a group "
"when the component is added (it has no element type: it is copied, like "
"\"My blocks\"). The impulse response comes later."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0025-declarative-components.md:37
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"**Checks** (`lumos.components.check_component`, `lumos component check "
"FILE`, the editor and the CI of the catalogue): the structure and the "
"identifier; a title, a description and a license; every parameter with a "
"unit (empty for dimensionless ones), a description and a default inside "
"its bounds; a body valid for the template, whose `\"$name\"` refer to "
"parameters of the right dimension; a passive behaviour unless declared "
"otherwise; the round trip through a `.lumos` document; **at least one "
"check with an independent reference value**, run each time: `{\"kind\": "
"\"power\", \"wavelength\", \"power\", \"expect\", \"rtol\"}` sends a beam"
" (or one guided lane per input of a matrix) of `power` and compares the "
"total output power with `expect`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0025-declarative-components.md:44
msgid ""
"**Registration**: `register_component(spec)` builds the element class "
"from the template (a pure transfer function closed over the body) and "
"registers it; registering the same definition again does nothing, another"
" definition under the same identifier and version is refused. A context "
"document using components embeds their definitions under `\"components\"`"
" (format 1.3), so that it opens anywhere."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0025-declarative-components.md:48
msgid ""
"**Code stays local**: components written in Python are plugins or script "
"blocks (ADR-0013), installed on local and private instances only (P15.15 "
"offers their code view there, never on the public instance)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0025-declarative-components.md:51
msgid "Alternatives considered"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0025-declarative-components.md:53
msgid ""
"**A safe expression language in the documents** (a formula for the "
"transfer): an interpreter to maintain and to secure, for a need the "
"templates cover."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0025-declarative-components.md:55
msgid ""
"**Components as Python only**: impossible on the public instance, where "
"the form editor is most useful."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0025-declarative-components.md:56
msgid ""
"**Composite components as element types**: a group already saves and "
"reloads itself; a type would add a dependency of the document on the "
"definition without benefit."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0025-declarative-components.md:59
msgid "Consequences"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0025-declarative-components.md:61
msgid ""
"A user builds a component in a form, checks it, shares its file, and "
"anyone opens it on any instance."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0025-declarative-components.md:62
msgid ""
"The behaviours are those of the templates; new templates are changes of "
"LUMOS, with their tests."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0025-declarative-components.md:63
msgid "The catalogue (P15.16) runs `lumos component check` on every contribution."
msgstr ""

